<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">United Nations Emergency Force</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1956">1956</a>–<a href="/years/1967">1967</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as UNEF · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suez-crisis">Suez Crisis</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> Emergency Force was the first armed peacekeeping force of the United Nations, created in November 1956 on the proposal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lester-b-pearson">Lester B. Pearson</a> to secure the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suez-crisis">Suez Crisis</a>. It supervised the withdrawal of British, French and Israeli forces and then patrolled the Egyptian–Israeli border in Sinai and Gaza until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> demanded its withdrawal in May 1967.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-nations-emergency-force.jpg" alt="United Nations Emergency Force" width="320" height="472" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government Press Office · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:UNEF_Yugoslav_soldiers_15-01-1957.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
